{"uid":"a1dc1fa0c773db76","name":"test_the_cure_pass_exemption_requires_the_diagnostic_now","fullName":"tests.test_engine_exit_wait_wiring#test_the_cure_pass_exemption_requires_the_diagnostic_now","historyId":"a716cfa73146b757fdff810e1dbef525","time":{"start":1791980731741,"stop":1791980731746,"duration":5},"description":"Task cure-01-07 (F.3/F.5, DoD 6): this guard used to stop at\n    FORBIDDING the helper -- it now also REQUIRES the reusable four-section\n    diagnostic be wired into the named node's own `except` clause. F.4/\n    non-negotiable 2 still binds exactly as it did (task 017's own\n    requirement): the named cure-pass node's single `proc.wait(timeout=60)`\n    stays unrouted (never `wait_engine_exit(...)` itself), unraised, and has\n    no barrier freshly inserted ahead of it -- the statement immediately\n    before the `try:` wrapping it, in the function body, is still the bare\n    `run = engine_factory(...)` assignment task 002 measured against,\n    nothing new in between. What is new: the wait must sit inside a `try:`\n    whose `except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:` handler raises an\n    `AssertionError` built from `engine_exit_timeout_diagnostic` (flowlib's\n    reusable dump builder) -- a bare `TimeoutExpired` escaping unhandled no\n    longer passes.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-07 (F.3/F.5, DoD 6): this guard used to stop at<br />\nFORBIDDING the helper -- it now also REQUIRES the reusable four-section<br />\ndiagnostic be wired into the named node's own <code>except</code> clause. F.4/<br />\nnon-negotiable 2 still binds exactly as it did (task 017's own<br />\nrequirement): the named cure-pass node's single <code>proc.wait(timeout=60)</code><br />\nstays unrouted (never <code>wait_engine_exit(...)</code> itself), unraised, and has<br />\nno barrier freshly inserted ahead of it -- the statement immediately<br />\nbefore the <code>try:</code> wrapping it, in the function body, is still the bare<br />\n<code>run = engine_factory(...)</c